<template>
<main class="cl anim-ready"><div class="bp-notice bp-notice-live" role="note"><div class="bp-notice-body"><span class="bp-notice-ca"><i aria-hidden="true"></i><span><a href="/token">$BP</a> contract<span class="bp-notice-chain"> on Robinhood Chain</span></span><button type="button" class="bp-ca" aria-label="Copy the contract address 0xB6F2e3D5f9F1BFb0363f3aECEC26B5B9bdbeEdC1"><code class="bp-ca-full">0xB6F2e3D5f9F1BFb0363f3aECEC26B5B9bdbeEdC1</code><code class="bp-ca-short">0xB6F2…EdC1</code><span class="bp-ca-act">Copy</span></button></span><span>Our only X account is <a href="https://x.com/agpool_robin" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@agpool_robin</a>.</span></div></div><header class="cl-nav"><div class="cl-nav-in"><a class="cl-brand" href="/"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" width="24" height="24" class="" aria-hidden="true"><defs><mask id="bp-mark-mask"><rect width="100" height="100" fill="#fff"></rect><path d="M50 20 L74 78 L61.5 78 L57 66 L43 66 L38.5 78 L26 78 Z M50 41 L53.5 58 L46.5 58 Z" fill="#000" fill-rule="evenodd"></path></mask></defs><rect width="100" height="100" rx="12" fill="currentColor" mask="url(#bp-mark-mask)"></rect></svg>Agpool<span class="cl-brand-sub">Changelog</span></a><nav class="cl-nav-links"><a href="/">Home</a><a href="/docs">Docs</a><a href="/agents">Agents</a><a href="/analytics">Analytics</a><a href="/recover">Recover</a></nav><a class="cl-btn" href="/app">Launch app</a></div></header><div class="cl-wrap"><div class="cl-head"><h1>Changelog</h1><p>New features and improvements to Agpool.</p></div><div class="cl-filter" role="tablist" aria-label="Filter by area"><button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true" class="on">All</button><button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" class="">Shield</button><button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" class="">Private send</button><button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" class="">Swap</button><button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" class="">Private bridge</button><button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" class="">Recovery</button><button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" class="">Analytics</button><button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" class="">CLI</button><button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" class="">Docs</button></div><div class="cl-list" data-area="all" data-ready=""><article class="cl-entry" id="token-launch" data-areas="docs" data-anim="" data-inview="" data-first=""><div class="cl-date"><span class="mono">Nov 10, 2026</span><i class="cl-dot"></i></div><div class="cl-body"><div class="cl-tags"><span class="cl-tag kind"><i></i>New feature</span><span class="cl-tag">Docs</span></div><h2><a href="#token-launch">$BP is live on Robinhood Chain</a></h2><p class="cl-lead">The Agpool token launched on the Orbio launchpad. Its contract address is at the top of agpool.cash and on agpool.cash/token.</p><div class="cl-vis"><div class="cl-mock"><div class="cl-mock-h">$BP<span>Robinhood Chain</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>contract</span><span>0xB6F2…EdC1</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>launchpad</span><span>Orbio</span></div></div></div><ul class="cl-bullets"><li>Contract: 0xB6F2e3D5f9F1BFb0363f3aECEC26B5B9bdbeEdC1 on Robinhood Chain (chain ID 4663).</li><li>Any other contract, airdrop or claim link is not ours.</li><li>Utility: soon.</li><li>Agpool works the same without the token; every fee is paid in the asset you move.</li></ul><div class="cl-links"><a class="cl-read" href="/token">Token page <span>→</span></a></div></div></article><article class="cl-entry" id="official-channels" data-areas="docs cli" data-anim="" data-inview=""><div class="cl-date"><span class="mono">Nov 9, 2026</span><i class="cl-dot"></i></div><div class="cl-body"><div class="cl-tags"><span class="cl-tag kind"><i></i>Improvement</span><span class="cl-tag">Docs</span><span class="cl-tag">CLI</span></div><h2><a href="#official-channels">Our only X account is @agpool_robin</a></h2><p class="cl-lead">Accounts pretending to be Agpool have appeared. Here is what is real.</p><div class="cl-vis"><div class="cl-mock"><div class="cl-mock-h">Official<span>channels</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>X</span><span class="cl-pill ok">@agpool_robin</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>website</span><span class="cl-pill ok">agpool.cash</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>token</span><span class="cl-pill ok">agpool.cash/token</span></div></div></div><ul class="cl-bullets"><li>The only official X account is @agpool_robin. It is linked from every page of agpool.cash, so you can always check it from here.</li><li>The Agpool token has one contract, shown at the top of agpool.cash and on agpool.cash/token. Any other token, airdrop or claim link using the Agpool name is not ours.</li><li>Agpool never asks for your recovery phrase or private key, and never messages you first.</li><li>CLI 0.4.6 carries the new description to npm and the MCP Registry; nothing else changes.</li></ul><div class="cl-links"><a class="cl-read" href="https://x.com/agpool_robin">@agpool_robin on X <span>→</span></a></div></div></article><article class="cl-entry" id="cli-0-4-5" data-areas="cli recovery send swap" data-anim="" data-inview=""><div class="cl-date"><span class="mono">Nov 9, 2026</span><i class="cl-dot"></i></div><div class="cl-body"><div class="cl-tags"><span class="cl-tag kind"><i></i>Improvement</span><span class="cl-tag">CLI</span><span class="cl-tag">Recovery</span><span class="cl-tag">Private send</span><span class="cl-tag">Swap</span></div><h2><a href="#cli-0-4-5">CLI 0.4.5 and steadier relaying on Robinhood Chain</a></h2><p class="cl-lead">A full test of every pool on every chain, through the CLI and the MCP server, found two problems. Both are fixed.</p><div class="cl-vis"><div class="cl-mock"><div class="cl-mock-h">CLI 0.4.5<span>recover</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>burner without gas</span><span class="cl-pill ok">topped up</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>stuck USDG swept</span><span class="cl-pill ok">done</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>duplicate relay sends</span><span class="cl-pill ok">gone</span></div></div></div><ul class="cl-bullets"><li>recover asks the relayer for a gas top-up when a one-time burner holds tokens but no gas, then sweeps it. Before, it asked you to send gas by hand.</li><li>recover no longer says every burner is clean while one still holds funds; the JSON result reports those in needsGas.</li><li>The relayer signs each transaction before it broadcasts it. When a node answers with an error although the transaction already went through, the relayer now uses that transaction instead of sending the same proof again, which made a successful payment look failed on Robinhood Chain.</li><li>Tested end to end with real funds: all nine pools, private sends through the CLI and the MCP server, swaps, bridges and recovery.</li></ul><div class="cl-links"><a class="cl-read" href="/docs#cli">CLI docs <span>→</span></a><a href="/AGENTS.md" class="cl-docs">Docs <span>↗</span></a></div></div></article><article class="cl-entry" id="mcp-registry-glama" data-areas="cli docs" data-anim="" data-inview=""><div class="cl-date"><span class="mono">Nov 6, 2026</span><i class="cl-dot"></i></div><div class="cl-body"><div class="cl-tags"><span class="cl-tag kind"><i></i>New feature</span><span class="cl-tag">CLI</span><span class="cl-tag">Docs</span></div><h2><a href="#mcp-registry-glama">The Agpool MCP server is listed on Glama and in the MCP Registry</a></h2><p class="cl-lead">AI agents can find Agpool by name in the official MCP Registry and on Glama, where both the local server and the hosted endpoint are verified listings.</p><div class="cl-vis"><div class="cl-mock"><div class="cl-mock-h">MCP server<span>listed</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>MCP Registry · cash.agpool/agpool</span><span class="cl-pill ok">listed</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>Glama · 9 tools</span><span class="cl-pill ok">verified</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>mcp.agpool.cash/mcp</span><span class="cl-pill ok">healthy</span></div></div></div><ul class="cl-bullets"><li>Listed in the official MCP Registry as cash.agpool/agpool, so MCP clients and directories can find it by name.</li><li>On Glama, the local server is built and tested from the open-source repository (9 tools, verified author) and the hosted read-only endpoint at mcp.agpool.cash/mcp has its ownership verified and is checked for health.</li><li>CLI 0.4.4 rewrites the tool descriptions for balance, assets and recover, so an agent picks the right tool and knows what each one returns.</li><li>The public repository now runs CodeQL code scanning and Dependabot security alerts on every change.</li></ul><div class="cl-links"><a class="cl-read" href="/agents">Agent guide <span>→</span></a><a href="/AGENTS.md" class="cl-docs">Docs <span>↗</span></a></div></div></article><article class="cl-entry" id="backup-rpcs" data-areas="send swap bridge" data-anim="" data-inview=""><div class="cl-date"><span class="mono">Nov 5, 2026</span><i class="cl-dot"></i></div><div class="cl-body"><div class="cl-tags"><span class="cl-tag kind"><i></i>Improvement</span><span class="cl-tag">Private send</span><span class="cl-tag">Swap</span><span class="cl-tag">Private bridge</span></div><h2><a href="#backup-rpcs">Private operations keep working when an RPC endpoint hangs</a></h2><p class="cl-lead">When a chain's RPC endpoint stops answering, the relayer now moves to a backup within seconds instead of failing the operation.</p><div class="cl-vis"><div class="cl-mock"><div class="cl-mock-h">Relayer RPC<span>Robinhood Chain</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>endpoint 1 · no answer in 15 s</span><span class="cl-pill">skipped</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>endpoint 2</span><span class="cl-pill ok">answered</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>private send</span><span class="cl-pill ok">relayed</span></div></div></div><ul class="cl-bullets"><li>Every chain has backup RPC endpoints. A request with no answer after 15 seconds moves to the next one, and an endpoint that fails is skipped for a minute.</li><li>On Robinhood Chain the backups now come first, after the main endpoint stopped answering for several minutes on November 5. Nothing was spent during that time: an operation the relayer cannot check first is refused, and the funds stay in the pool.</li><li>The status page answers in about a second even when one chain is slow, and monitoring now alerts when the API is slow, not only when it is unreachable.</li></ul><div class="cl-links"><a class="cl-read" href="/status">Open status <span>→</span></a></div></div></article><article class="cl-entry" id="cli-0-4-3" data-areas="cli swap send" data-anim="" hidden=""><div class="cl-date"><span class="mono">Nov 4, 2026</span><i class="cl-dot"></i></div><div class="cl-body"><div class="cl-tags"><span class="cl-tag kind"><i></i>Improvement</span><span class="cl-tag">CLI</span><span class="cl-tag">Swap</span><span class="cl-tag">Private send</span></div><h2><a href="#cli-0-4-3">CLI 0.4.3: swap fixes from a second full test run</a></h2><p class="cl-lead">A second run of every flow with real funds on all four chains turned up three edge cases, all fixed here and in the web app.</p><div class="cl-vis"><div class="cl-mock"><div class="cl-mock-h">CLI 0.4.3<span>fixes</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>swap max --from usdt --chain bsc</span><span class="cl-pill ok">fixed</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>swap max --from usdc --chain base</span><span class="cl-pill ok">fixed</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>burner after swap</span><span class="cl-pill ok">empty</span></div></div></div><ul class="cl-bullets"><li>Stablecoin to BNB swaps on BNB Chain work from the CLI (they stopped with "unknown pool").</li><li>Stablecoin to ETH swaps wait until the unwrapped ETH is visible before re-shielding it, so a public RPC node a block behind can no longer shrink the re-shield.</li><li>The unused gas on a one-time burner is returned reliably on Base: the balance is read at the re-shield's block and the transfer retries with a fresh balance.</li><li>send max waits and tries again when the balance view is a moment behind a send that just happened.</li></ul><div class="cl-links"><a class="cl-read" href="/docs#cli">CLI docs <span>→</span></a><a href="/AGENTS.md" class="cl-docs">Docs <span>↗</span></a></div></div></article><article class="cl-entry" id="cli-0-4-2" data-areas="cli swap send" data-anim="" hidden=""><div class="cl-date"><span class="mono">Nov 4, 2026</span><i class="cl-dot"></i></div><div class="cl-body"><div class="cl-tags"><span class="cl-tag kind"><i></i>Improvement</span><span class="cl-tag">CLI</span><span class="cl-tag">Swap</span><span class="cl-tag">Private send</span></div><h2><a href="#cli-0-4-2">CLI 0.4.2: max amounts and swaps that leave nothing behind</a></h2><p class="cl-lead">Every flow was run end to end with real funds on Robinhood Chain, Base, Arbitrum and BNB Chain; this release carries what that run fixed.</p><div class="cl-vis"><div class="cl-mock"><div class="cl-mock-h">CLI 0.4.2<span>4 chains tested</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>send 0x… max --chain all</span><span class="cl-pill ok">every pool</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>swap 0.002 ETH → USDC</span><span class="cl-pill ok">burner empty</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>Robinhood · Base · Arbitrum · BNB</span><span class="cl-pill ok">passed</span></div></div></div><ul class="cl-bullets"><li>send, swap and bridge accept max. send max empties a pool, every pool on a chain, or every pool on every chain (--chain all), splitting across several sends when the balance sits in many notes.</li><li>Private swaps swap the full amount. The relayer advances the gas to re-shield the output and the one-time burner returns what it did not use, so no funds stay behind; the web app does the same.</li><li>The CLI exits as soon as a command finishes, prices gas from the live base fee (Arbitrum no longer fails with "cannot estimate gas"), sends a valid gas price on BNB Chain, and passes exact amounts, so a full balance of an 18-decimal token can be sent.</li><li>Balances read right after a transaction are current: the API checks every pool snapshot against the chain before answering.</li><li>Two open app tabs can no longer recover the same burner at once, and every recovery is simulated before it is sent.</li></ul><div class="cl-links"><a class="cl-read" href="/docs#cli">CLI docs <span>→</span></a><a href="/AGENTS.md" class="cl-docs">Docs <span>↗</span></a></div></div></article><article class="cl-entry" id="bridges-in-wallet" data-areas="bridge" data-anim="" hidden=""><div class="cl-date"><span class="mono">Nov 3, 2026</span><i class="cl-dot"></i></div><div class="cl-body"><div class="cl-tags"><span class="cl-tag kind"><i></i>Improvement</span><span class="cl-tag">Private bridge</span></div><h2><a href="#bridges-in-wallet">Private bridges in the wallet panel</a></h2><p class="cl-lead">Open the wallet button to see your private bridges; the form keeps one line while a bridge is running.</p><div class="cl-vis"><div class="cl-mock"><div class="cl-mock-h">Wallet<span>Private bridges</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>0.004 ETH Arbitrum → Base</span><span class="cl-pill pend">Bridging</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>0.00657 ETH Base → Robinhood</span><span class="cl-pill ok">Delivered</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>History &amp; recovery</span><span class="cl-pill ok">/recover</span></div></div></div><ul class="cl-bullets"><li>The wallet button shows how many bridges are in flight. Its panel lists the latest bridges with status, amount received and a Track link, plus History &amp; recovery for older ones.</li><li>On phones the panel opens as a sheet from the bottom of the screen.</li><li>While a bridge runs, a single line above the form shows it; a delivered bridge stays there for a few minutes.</li></ul><div class="cl-links"><a class="cl-read" href="/app">Open the app <span>→</span></a><a href="/docs" class="cl-docs">Docs <span>↗</span></a></div></div></article><article class="cl-entry" id="lower-bnb-minimum" data-areas="shield bridge cli" data-anim="" hidden=""><div class="cl-date"><span class="mono">Nov 3, 2026</span><i class="cl-dot"></i></div><div class="cl-body"><div class="cl-tags"><span class="cl-tag kind"><i></i>Improvement</span><span class="cl-tag">Shield</span><span class="cl-tag">Private bridge</span><span class="cl-tag">CLI</span></div><h2><a href="#lower-bnb-minimum">Lower BNB minimum, steadier network switching</a></h2><p class="cl-lead">Shielding into the BNB pool now starts at 0.01 BNB, and switching networks no longer gets stuck.</p><div class="cl-vis"><div class="cl-mock"><div class="cl-mock-h">BNB pool<span>BNB Chain</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>Minimum deposit</span><span class="cl-pill ok">0.01 BNB</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>Withdraw fee</span><span class="cl-pill pend">0.001 + 0.35%</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>Network switch</span><span class="cl-pill ok">no more stuck</span></div></div></div><ul class="cl-bullets"><li>The minimum deposit for the BNB pool is 0.01 BNB, down from 0.02. The withdraw fee at the minimum is about 10%; the other pools are unchanged.</li><li>The network button asks the wallet directly and reads its real network afterwards, so it no longer stays on "Switching..." with wallets that skip the network-change event. A cancelled or unanswered switch shows a short note.</li><li>The running step in the progress window has a new animation, and a delivered bridge is shown once, in the Recent bridges card.</li><li>CLI 0.4.1 applies the same BNB minimum.</li></ul><div class="cl-links"><a class="cl-read" href="/app">Open the app <span>→</span></a><a href="/docs#fees" class="cl-docs">Docs <span>↗</span></a></div></div></article><article class="cl-entry" id="safe-admin" data-areas="shield send swap bridge" data-anim="" hidden=""><div class="cl-date"><span class="mono">Nov 3, 2026</span><i class="cl-dot"></i></div><div class="cl-body"><div class="cl-tags"><span class="cl-tag kind"><i></i>Improvement</span><span class="cl-tag">Shield</span><span class="cl-tag">Private send</span><span class="cl-tag">Swap</span><span class="cl-tag">Private bridge</span></div><h2><a href="#safe-admin">Pools controlled by a multisig</a></h2><p class="cl-lead">Upgrading or pausing any pool now takes two of three independent signatures.</p><div class="cl-vis"><div class="cl-mock"><div class="cl-mock-h">Admin<span>Safe · 2 of 3</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>Robinhood · Base · Arbitrum · BNB</span><span class="cl-pill ok">same Safe</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>Upgrade or pause</span><span class="cl-pill pend">2 signatures</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>Move user notes</span><span class="cl-pill ok">impossible</span></div></div></div><ul class="cl-bullets"><li>Every pool on Robinhood Chain, Base, Arbitrum and BNB Chain is administered by one Safe, 0x401027251176A8AFec701fE37412edeC45ec6FdB, the same address on all four chains.</li><li>The launch admin key handed over and holds no rights. The admin still cannot move notes; it can only pause or upgrade, now with two signatures.</li></ul><div class="cl-links"><a class="cl-read" href="/docs#security">Read the security model <span>→</span></a><a href="/docs#contracts" class="cl-docs">Docs <span>↗</span></a></div></div></article><article class="cl-entry" id="client-side-proving" data-areas="shield send swap bridge cli" data-anim="" hidden=""><div class="cl-date"><span class="mono">Nov 3, 2026</span><i class="cl-dot"></i></div><div class="cl-body"><div class="cl-tags"><span class="cl-tag kind"><i></i>New feature</span><span class="cl-tag">Shield</span><span class="cl-tag">Private send</span><span class="cl-tag">Swap</span><span class="cl-tag">Private bridge</span><span class="cl-tag">CLI</span></div><h2><a href="#client-side-proving">Client-side proving</a></h2><p class="cl-lead">Your keys and every zero-knowledge proof stay on your device. The relayer only ever sees finished proofs.</p><div class="cl-vis"><div class="cl-mock"><div class="cl-mock-h">Proving<span>groth16 · on this device</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>Keys and notes</span><span class="cl-pill ok">this device</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>Proof</span><span class="cl-pill ok">this device</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>Relayer receives</span><span class="cl-pill pend">proof only</span></div></div></div><ul class="cl-bullets"><li>The web app proves in a background worker and CLI 0.4.0 proves in Node. Your sign-in signature is never sent anywhere; your balance is computed on your device from public pool data.</li><li>The relayer checks its fee, simulates and broadcasts the finished proof, so it cannot change the recipient or the amount. The proving key (about 20 MB) downloads once and is checked against its SHA-256.</li><li>No browser storage: wallet state, keys and notes live in memory and are gone when the tab closes.</li></ul><div class="cl-links"><a class="cl-read" href="/docs#security">Read the security model <span>→</span></a><a href="/docs#api" class="cl-docs">Docs <span>↗</span></a></div></div></article><article class="cl-entry" id="mcp-servers" data-areas="cli docs" data-anim="" hidden=""><div class="cl-date"><span class="mono">Nov 3, 2026</span><i class="cl-dot"></i></div><div class="cl-body"><div class="cl-tags"><span class="cl-tag kind"><i></i>New feature</span><span class="cl-tag">CLI</span><span class="cl-tag">Docs</span></div><h2><a href="#mcp-servers">MCP servers</a></h2><p class="cl-lead">Agent apps can use Agpool as tools over the Model Context Protocol, no shell required.</p><div class="cl-vis"><div class="cl-mock"><div class="cl-mock-h">MCP<span>stdio · streamable HTTP</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span class="mono">agpool_balance</span><span class="cl-pill ok">read-only</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span class="mono">agpool_send</span><span class="cl-pill pend">destructive</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span class="mono">agpool_bridge_quote</span><span class="cl-pill ok">hosted</span></div></div></div><ul class="cl-bullets"><li>Local server in the CLI (npx -y @agpool/cli@latest mcp): balance, deposit, send, swap, bridge, bridges, assets and recover, with the wallet key kept on your machine and an allow-list per tool.</li><li>Hosted read-only server at mcp.agpool.cash/mcp: status, fees and minimums, bridge assets and quotes, analytics and the agent guide.</li></ul><div class="cl-links"><a class="cl-read" href="/agents#9-mcp-servers">Set it up <span>→</span></a><a href="/AGENTS.md" class="cl-docs">Docs <span>↗</span></a></div></div></article><article class="cl-entry" id="built-for-agents" data-areas="cli docs" data-anim="" hidden=""><div class="cl-date"><span class="mono">Nov 3, 2026</span><i class="cl-dot"></i></div><div class="cl-body"><div class="cl-tags"><span class="cl-tag kind"><i></i>New feature</span><span class="cl-tag">CLI</span><span class="cl-tag">Docs</span></div><h2><a href="#built-for-agents">Built for agents</a></h2><p class="cl-lead">CLI 0.2.0 speaks JSON, and AGENTS.md tells an agent everything it needs in one file.</p><div class="cl-vis"><div class="cl-mock"><div class="cl-mock-h">Agent<span>@agpool/cli 0.2.0 · --json</span></div><div class="cl-code"><span class="c">$</span> agpool send 0x9f3c…41e7 10 --pool usdc --json</div><div class="cl-code">{"ok":true,"command":"send","received":"8.965","symbol":"USDC"}</div><div class="cl-status ok">exit 0 · relayer paid the gas</div></div></div><ul class="cl-bullets"><li>--json prints one object on stdout with stable fields per command; progress goes to stderr; exit codes 0, 1 and 2.</li><li>New: agpool address, bridge --no-wait, AGPOOL_HOME, automatic waits on rate limits. AGENTS.md lives at agpool.cash/AGENTS.md and ships inside the npm package.</li></ul><div class="cl-links"><a class="cl-read" href="/docs#agents">Read the agent guide <span>→</span></a><a href="/AGENTS.md" class="cl-docs">Docs <span>↗</span></a></div></div></article><article class="cl-entry" id="sign-in-message-v2" data-areas="shield" data-anim="" hidden=""><div class="cl-date"><span class="mono">Nov 3, 2026</span><i class="cl-dot"></i></div><div class="cl-body"><div class="cl-tags"><span class="cl-tag kind"><i></i>Improvement</span><span class="cl-tag">Shield</span></div><h2><a href="#sign-in-message-v2">A sign-in message that says what it does</a></h2><p class="cl-lead">The message you sign now states that your private account keys are derived from it, and where it is safe to sign.</p><div class="cl-vis"><div class="cl-mock"><div class="cl-mock-h">Signature request<span>agpool.cash</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>Gas free: no transaction is sent</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>Your private account keys are derived from this signature</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>Only sign it on agpool.cash or the Agpool CLI</span></div></div></div><ul class="cl-bullets"><li>It cannot move funds from your wallet or approve spending, and you should only sign it on agpool.cash or the Agpool CLI.</li><li>Accounts are derived from the message, so this is a new account space; it shipped before any public deposits.</li></ul><div class="cl-links"><a class="cl-read" href="/app">Launch app <span>→</span></a><a href="/docs#concepts" class="cl-docs">Docs <span>↗</span></a></div></div></article><article class="cl-entry" id="status-privacy-terms" data-areas="docs" data-anim="" hidden=""><div class="cl-date"><span class="mono">Nov 3, 2026</span><i class="cl-dot"></i></div><div class="cl-body"><div class="cl-tags"><span class="cl-tag kind"><i></i>New feature</span><span class="cl-tag">Docs</span></div><h2><a href="#status-privacy-terms">Status, privacy and terms</a></h2><p class="cl-lead">A live status page, and plain answers to what Agpool processes and stores.</p><div class="cl-vis"><div class="cl-mock"><div class="cl-mock-h">Status<span>checked from your browser</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>Relayer API</span><span class="cl-pill ok">operational</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>Indexer</span><span class="cl-pill ok">operational</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>Robinhood Chain · relayer gas</span><span class="cl-pill ok">funded</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>BNB Chain · RPC</span><span class="cl-pill ok">operational</span></div></div></div><ul class="cl-bullets"><li>Status checks the relayer API, the indexer, relayer gas and every chain's RPC from your browser each time it loads.</li><li>Privacy lists exactly what the API receives, the three things it stores and what is public on-chain. The docs now describe server-assisted proving, admin key and audit status as they are.</li></ul><div class="cl-links"><a class="cl-read" href="/status">Open status <span>→</span></a><a href="/privacy" class="cl-docs">Docs <span>↗</span></a></div></div></article><article class="cl-entry" id="analytics-by-day" data-areas="analytics" data-anim="" hidden=""><div class="cl-date"><span class="mono">Nov 3, 2026</span><i class="cl-dot"></i></div><div class="cl-body"><div class="cl-tags"><span class="cl-tag kind"><i></i>Improvement</span><span class="cl-tag">Analytics</span></div><h2><a href="#analytics-by-day">Analytics by day</a></h2><p class="cl-lead">Every shielded note is now dated by its block, so activity shows per day while the pools are young.</p><div class="cl-vis"><div class="cl-mock wide"><div class="cl-tiles"><div><span>Shielded notes</span><b>14</b></div><div><span>Relayer fees</span><b>$1.27</b></div><div><span>Chains</span><b>4</b></div></div><div class="cl-mock-f">First day of live data on Robinhood Chain</div></div></div><ul class="cl-bullets"><li>The activity chart switches from days to months on its own once there is more than six weeks of history.</li><li>Pools show their latest indexed block, and relayer fees are shown in USD next to the exact per-token amounts.</li></ul><div class="cl-links"><a class="cl-read" href="/analytics">Open analytics <span>→</span></a></div></div></article><article class="cl-entry" id="wallet-network" data-areas="shield" data-anim="" hidden=""><div class="cl-date"><span class="mono">Nov 3, 2026</span><i class="cl-dot"></i></div><div class="cl-body"><div class="cl-tags"><span class="cl-tag kind"><i></i>Improvement</span><span class="cl-tag">Shield</span></div><h2><a href="#wallet-network">Follows your wallet's network</a></h2><p class="cl-lead">The app no longer shows one chain while your wallet sits on another.</p><div class="cl-vis"><div class="cl-mock"><div class="cl-mock-h">Shield<span>wallet on Ethereum mainnet</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>Your wallet is on an unsupported network</span><span class="cl-pill pend">switch</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span><i class="cl-chk">✓</i>Switched to Robinhood Chain</span></div><div class="cl-status ok">Deposit confirmed · 0.001 ETH shielded</div></div></div><ul class="cl-bullets"><li>On connect, a wallet on an unsupported network is asked to switch to Robinhood Chain; every deposit checks the network again before you sign.</li><li>If you decline, the network switcher says so and a banner offers a one-click switch. Deposits on Robinhood Chain confirm in seconds.</li></ul><div class="cl-links"><a class="cl-read" href="/app">Open in app <span>→</span></a><a href="/docs#shield" class="cl-docs">Docs <span>↗</span></a></div></div></article><article class="cl-entry" id="relayer-reliability" data-areas="send swap bridge" data-anim="" hidden=""><div class="cl-date"><span class="mono">Nov 3, 2026</span><i class="cl-dot"></i></div><div class="cl-body"><div class="cl-tags"><span class="cl-tag kind"><i></i>Improvement</span><span class="cl-tag">Private send</span><span class="cl-tag">Swap</span><span class="cl-tag">Private bridge</span></div><h2><a href="#relayer-reliability">Steadier relayer</a></h2><p class="cl-lead">Long flows no longer stop half-way because of our own limits.</p><div class="cl-vis"><div class="cl-mock"><div class="cl-mock-h">Private bridge<span>Robinhood Chain → Base</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span><i class="cl-chk">✓</i>Generate proof</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span><i class="cl-chk">✓</i>Bridge via NEAR Intents</span><span class="mono">retried after 4 s</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span class="cur">Delivering to recipient</span><span class="cl-pill run">running</span></div></div></div><ul class="cl-bullets"><li>Rate limits count what an operation costs, not its HTTP method; the app waits and retries when it is told to slow down.</li><li>Relayer broadcasts queue per chain, so simultaneous sends never collide on a nonce, and bridge minimums read in tokens, not raw units.</li></ul><div class="cl-links"><a class="cl-read" href="/app">Open in app <span>→</span></a><a href="/docs#api" class="cl-docs">Docs <span>↗</span></a></div></div></article><article class="cl-entry" id="cli-on-npm" data-areas="cli" data-anim="" hidden=""><div class="cl-date"><span class="mono">Nov 3, 2026</span><i class="cl-dot"></i></div><div class="cl-body"><div class="cl-tags"><span class="cl-tag kind"><i></i>New feature</span><span class="cl-tag">CLI</span></div><h2><a href="#cli-on-npm">The CLI is on npm</a></h2><p class="cl-lead">@agpool/cli gives scripts and agents the same private payments as the app.</p><div class="cl-vis"><div class="cl-mock"><div class="cl-mock-h">Terminal<span>@agpool/cli 0.1.0</span></div><div class="cl-code"><span class="c">$</span> npm i -g @agpool/cli</div><div class="cl-code"><span class="c">$</span> agpool balance --chain robinhood</div><div class="cl-code"><span class="c">$</span> agpool recover --chain all</div></div></div><ul class="cl-bullets"><li>Install with npm i -g @agpool/cli, or run it once with npx @agpool/cli help.</li><li>Balance, shield, send, swap, bridge and recover on all four chains; --chain all sweeps every chain in one go.</li></ul><div class="cl-links"><a class="cl-read" href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@agpool/cli">View on npm <span>→</span></a><a href="/docs#cli" class="cl-docs">Docs <span>↗</span></a></div></div></article><article class="cl-entry" id="recover-redesign" data-areas="recovery" data-anim="" hidden=""><div class="cl-date"><span class="mono">Nov 3, 2026</span><i class="cl-dot"></i></div><div class="cl-body"><div class="cl-tags"><span class="cl-tag kind"><i></i>Improvement</span><span class="cl-tag">Recovery</span></div><h2><a href="#recover-redesign">A new Recover page</a></h2><p class="cl-lead">One signature, four chains, every burner you ever registered.</p><div class="cl-vis"><div class="cl-mock"><div class="cl-mock-h">Recover funds<span>Robinhood Chain · Base · Arbitrum · BNB Chain</span></div><div class="cl-kv"><span>Signature</span><b>1 · stays in this browser</b></div><div class="cl-kv"><span>Burner registry</span><b>decrypted locally</b></div><div class="cl-status ok">2 burners swept back to your wallet</div></div></div><ul class="cl-bullets"><li>Recover reads the encrypted burner registry page by page, so there is no cap on how many burners an account can have.</li><li>The legacy fixed-slot scan is gone: fewer RPC calls, faster results.</li></ul><div class="cl-links"><a class="cl-read" href="/recover">Open recovery <span>→</span></a><a href="/docs#recovery" class="cl-docs">Docs <span>↗</span></a></div></div></article><article class="cl-entry" id="four-chains-live" data-areas="shield send" data-anim="" hidden=""><div class="cl-date"><span class="mono">Nov 2, 2026</span><i class="cl-dot"></i></div><div class="cl-body"><div class="cl-tags"><span class="cl-tag kind"><i></i>New feature</span><span class="cl-tag">Shield</span><span class="cl-tag">Private send</span></div><h2><a href="#four-chains-live">Live on four chains</a></h2><p class="cl-lead">Nine pools on Robinhood Chain, Base, Arbitrum and BNB Chain, every contract source-verified.</p><div class="cl-vis"><div class="cl-mock"><div class="cl-mock-h">Pools<span>9 live</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>Robinhood Chain</span><span class="mono">ETH · USDG</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>Base</span><span class="mono">ETH · USDC</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>Arbitrum</span><span class="mono">ETH · USDC</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>BNB Chain</span><span class="mono">BNB · USDC · USDT</span></div></div></div><ul class="cl-bullets"><li>ETH and USDG on Robinhood Chain, ETH and USDC on Base and Arbitrum, BNB, USDC and USDT on BNB Chain.</li><li>All implementations are verified on Sourcify; the full address book is in the docs.</li></ul><div class="cl-links"><a class="cl-read" href="/app">Launch app <span>→</span></a><a href="/docs#contracts" class="cl-docs">Docs <span>↗</span></a></div></div></article><article class="cl-entry" id="one-signature" data-areas="recovery shield" data-anim="" hidden=""><div class="cl-date"><span class="mono">Nov 2, 2026</span><i class="cl-dot"></i></div><div class="cl-body"><div class="cl-tags"><span class="cl-tag kind"><i></i>Improvement</span><span class="cl-tag">Recovery</span><span class="cl-tag">Shield</span></div><h2><a href="#one-signature">One signature</a></h2><p class="cl-lead">Signing in now takes a single wallet prompt, in the app, on Recover and in the CLI.</p><div class="cl-vis"><div class="cl-mock"><div class="cl-mock-h">Sign in<span>1 of 1</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>Welcome to Agpool</span><span class="cl-pill ok">signed</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span>Registry access</span><span class="mono">derived, no prompt</span></div></div></div><ul class="cl-bullets"><li>The registry signature is derived from your sign-in signature instead of asking the wallet a second time.</li><li>The sign-in message says what it does: no transaction, your private keys come from it, it cannot touch your wallet, and where to sign it.</li></ul><div class="cl-links"><a class="cl-read" href="/app">Launch app <span>→</span></a><a href="/docs#concepts" class="cl-docs">Docs <span>↗</span></a></div></div></article><article class="cl-entry" id="private-bridge-routes" data-areas="bridge" data-anim="" hidden=""><div class="cl-date"><span class="mono">Nov 2, 2026</span><i class="cl-dot"></i></div><div class="cl-body"><div class="cl-tags"><span class="cl-tag kind"><i></i>New feature</span><span class="cl-tag">Private bridge</span></div><h2><a href="#private-bridge-routes">Private bridge routes</a></h2><p class="cl-lead">Bridge a shielded note to Solana, Ethereum, Base, Arbitrum or Robinhood Chain through NEAR Intents.</p><div class="cl-vis"><div class="cl-mock"><div class="cl-mock-h">Bridge privately<span>From Robinhood Chain · private ETH</span></div><div class="cl-route"><span class="cl-chip"><img src="/token_logos/robinhood.png?v=2" alt="">Robinhood</span><i class="cl-line"></i><span class="cl-chip">NEAR Intents</span><i class="cl-line"></i><span class="cl-chip dst"><img src="/token_logos/solana.png" alt="">Solana</span></div><div class="cl-kv"><span>Recipient</span><b class="mono">7Gx4…kQ2m</b></div><div class="cl-kv"><span>You receive</span><b>≈ 2,259 USDC</b></div><div class="cl-status ok">Delivered on Solana · no trail</div></div></div><ul class="cl-bullets"><li>The proof pays a one-time burner; the burner funds a one-off 1Click deposit address, so the origin chain never carries the recipient.</li><li>Every intent is written to your encrypted registry, so a bridge that stalls mid-way is recoverable from any device.</li></ul><div class="cl-links"><a class="cl-read" href="/app">Open in app <span>→</span></a><a href="/docs#bridge" class="cl-docs">Docs <span>↗</span></a></div></div></article><article class="cl-entry" id="public-analytics" data-areas="analytics" data-anim="" hidden=""><div class="cl-date"><span class="mono">Nov 2, 2026</span><i class="cl-dot"></i></div><div class="cl-body"><div class="cl-tags"><span class="cl-tag kind"><i></i>New feature</span><span class="cl-tag">Analytics</span></div><h2><a href="#public-analytics">Public analytics</a></h2><p class="cl-lead">Protocol numbers derived only from data that is already on-chain.</p><div class="cl-vis"><div class="cl-mock wide"><div class="cl-tiles"><div><span>Shielded notes</span><b>12,480</b></div><div><span>Pools</span><b>7</b></div><div><span>Chains</span><b>4</b></div></div><div class="cl-bars"><div><span>Base</span><i style="width:100%;background:#4C7FE3"></i><b>6,214</b></div><div><span>Robinhood Chain</span><i style="width:58%;background:#27A563"></i><b>3,590</b></div><div><span>Arbitrum</span><i style="width:31%;background:#7B68E0"></i><b>1,902</b></div><div><span>BNB Chain</span><i style="width:12%;background:#C2842A"></i><b>774</b></div></div><div class="cl-mock-f">Illustrative numbers · live data populates from the first shielded note</div></div></div><ul class="cl-bullets"><li>Shielded notes, pools, chains and relayer fees, refreshed every minute from the indexer.</li><li>No TVL in USD, by design: deposit amounts are encrypted on-chain, so a pool-wide total cannot be verified and is not shown.</li></ul><div class="cl-links"><a class="cl-read" href="/analytics">Open analytics <span>→</span></a><a href="/docs#api" class="cl-docs">Docs <span>↗</span></a></div></div></article><article class="cl-entry" id="documentation" data-areas="docs" data-anim="" hidden=""><div class="cl-date"><span class="mono">Nov 2, 2026</span><i class="cl-dot"></i></div><div class="cl-body"><div class="cl-tags"><span class="cl-tag kind"><i></i>New feature</span><span class="cl-tag">Docs</span></div><h2><a href="#documentation">Documentation</a></h2><p class="cl-lead">Thirteen anchored sections, from core concepts to the security model.</p><div class="cl-vis"><div class="cl-mock"><div class="cl-mock-h">Docs<span>agpool.cash/docs</span></div><div class="cl-chips"><span class="cl-chip">Overview</span><span class="cl-chip">Core concepts</span><span class="cl-chip">Shield</span><span class="cl-chip">Private send</span><span class="cl-chip">Swap</span><span class="cl-chip on">Private bridge</span><span class="cl-chip">Recovery</span><span class="cl-chip">Chains &amp; assets</span><span class="cl-chip">Fees</span><span class="cl-chip">CLI</span><span class="cl-chip">API</span><span class="cl-chip">Security model</span><span class="cl-chip">FAQ</span></div><div class="cl-code"><span class="c">$</span> agpool bridge --chain robinhood --to solana --amount 1 ETH</div></div></div><ul class="cl-bullets"><li>Shield, Private send, Swap, Private bridge and Recovery each get a walk-through plus the exact relayer endpoints behind them.</li><li>Fees, chains &amp; assets and the CLI reference live on the same page, so every section is linkable.</li></ul><div class="cl-links"><a class="cl-read" href="/docs">Read the docs <span>→</span></a></div></div></article><article class="cl-entry" id="deterministic-recovery" data-areas="recovery bridge" data-anim="" hidden=""><div class="cl-date"><span class="mono">Nov 1, 2026</span><i class="cl-dot"></i></div><div class="cl-body"><div class="cl-tags"><span class="cl-tag kind"><i></i>New feature</span><span class="cl-tag">Recovery</span><span class="cl-tag">Private bridge</span></div><h2><a href="#deterministic-recovery">Recovery from any device</a></h2><p class="cl-lead">Every burner and bridge is recoverable from your signature alone, on any device.</p><div class="cl-vis"><div class="cl-mock"><div class="cl-mock-h">Recovery<span>unlocked by one signature</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span class="mono">burner 0x4a1e…c0d2</span><span class="cl-pill ok">swept</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span class="mono">burner 0x77b0…9e1f</span><span class="cl-pill pend">empty</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span class="mono">bridge → Solana · 1Click</span><span class="cl-pill ok">delivered</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span class="mono cur">bridge → Base · 1Click</span><span class="cl-pill run">pending</span></div></div></div><ul class="cl-bullets"><li>Every burner is registered, encrypted in your browser, before it is funded; the registry lists every burner and intent you ever created.</li><li>Sweep a stuck burner or check an intent's status from any device. The registry only ever stores ciphertext.</li></ul><div class="cl-links"><a class="cl-read" href="/recover">Open recovery <span>→</span></a><a href="/docs#recovery" class="cl-docs">Docs <span>↗</span></a></div></div></article><article class="cl-entry" id="swap-inside-the-pool" data-areas="swap" data-anim="" hidden=""><div class="cl-date"><span class="mono">Nov 1, 2026</span><i class="cl-dot"></i></div><div class="cl-body"><div class="cl-tags"><span class="cl-tag kind"><i></i>New feature</span><span class="cl-tag">Swap</span></div><h2><a href="#swap-inside-the-pool">Swap inside the pool</a></h2><p class="cl-lead">Trade ETH ⇄ USDC through Uniswap V3 and settle back into the pool privately.</p><div class="cl-vis"><div class="cl-mock"><div class="cl-mock-h">Swap<span>Uniswap V3 · one-time burner · re-shielded</span></div><div class="cl-swap"><span class="cl-tok"><img src="/token_logos/eth.png" alt="">0.5 ETH</span><span class="cl-arrow">⇄</span><span class="cl-tok"><img src="/token_logos/usdc.png" alt="">1,134 USDC</span></div><div class="cl-status ok">Re-shielded · private balance updated</div></div></div><ul class="cl-bullets"><li>A one-time burner executes the trade, then the output is re-shielded as a fresh note.</li><li>Nothing on-chain links the trade to your deposit.</li></ul><div class="cl-links"><a class="cl-read" href="/app">Open in app <span>→</span></a><a href="/docs#swap" class="cl-docs">Docs <span>↗</span></a></div></div></article><article class="cl-entry" id="introducing-agpool" data-areas="shield send" data-anim="" hidden=""><div class="cl-date"><span class="mono">Nov 1, 2026</span><i class="cl-dot"></i></div><div class="cl-body"><div class="cl-tags"><span class="cl-tag kind"><i></i>New feature</span><span class="cl-tag">Shield</span><span class="cl-tag">Private send</span></div><h2><a href="#introducing-agpool">Introducing Agpool</a></h2><p class="cl-lead">Private payments that leave no trail: per-token anonymity pools on Base, Robinhood Chain, Arbitrum and BNB Chain.</p><div class="cl-vis"><div class="cl-mock"><div class="cl-mock-h">Private balance<span>1.284 ETH on Base</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span><i class="cl-chk">✓</i>Note encrypted to your account</span><span class="mono">Shield</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span><i class="cl-chk">✓</i>Commitment added to the Merkle tree</span></div><div class="cl-row"><span><i class="cl-chk">✓</i>Sent to 0x9f3c…41e7 · relayer paid gas</span><span class="mono">Send</span></div><div class="cl-progress"><i></i></div></div></div><ul class="cl-bullets"><li>No fixed denominations, no mixer queues, no waiting periods. Any amount, whenever you want it back.</li><li>The relayer builds the proof and pays the gas, so your wallet never touches the spend.</li></ul><div class="cl-links"><a class="cl-read" href="/app">Launch app <span>→</span></a><a href="/docs#overview" class="cl-docs">Docs <span>↗</span></a></div></div></article><p class="cl-empty">Nothing in this area yet.</p></div><nav class="cl-pager" aria-label="Changelog pages"><button type="button" class="cl-pg-step" aria-label="Newer entries" disabled=""><span aria-hidden="true">←</span><span class="cl-pg-word">Newer</span></button><div class="cl-pg-nums"><button type="button" class="on" aria-current="page" aria-label="Page 1">1</button><button type="button" class="" aria-label="Page 2">2</button><button type="button" class="" aria-label="Page 3">3</button><button type="button" class="" aria-label="Page 4">4</button><button type="button" class="" aria-label="Page 5">5</button><button type="button" class="" aria-label="Page 6">6</button></div><button type="button" class="cl-pg-step" aria-label="Older entries"><span class="cl-pg-word">Older</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button></nav><section class="cl-cta"><h2>Move value privately.<br><span>Start with one signature.</span></h2><p>Connect a wallet, sign once, and your private account exists on every supported chain.</p><a class="cl-btn lg" href="/app">Launch app</a></section><p class="cl-foot">© 2026 Agpool. Dates reflect when each capability went live on agpool.cash.</p></div></main>
</template>

